From 5138aa41183c0790218be6e87928f038613b2b96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <dev@phlink.local>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:46:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 10.03 macOS update helper
 (phlink_update_helper)

Adds a standalone Mach-O executable, phlink_update_helper, that applies
a staged update on next launch:

  phlink_update_helper --apply <staging_dir> <target_app_path>

Pipeline:
  1. Read & validate staged.json (StagedPayload schema v1).
  2. Confirm payload zip exists on disk.
  3. Refuse to in-place-update an ad-hoc-signed .app (D-08): inspects
     kSecCodeInfoTeamIdentifier + kSecCodeSignatureAdhoc flag via
     SecStaticCodeCreateWithPath + SecCodeCopySigningInformation.
  4. Extract zip via /usr/bin/ditto -xk into a temp dir under the
     staging dir.
  5. SecStaticCodeCheckValidity on the extracted .app with
     kSecCSCheckAllArchitectures | kSecCSCheckNestedCode |
     kSecCSStrictValidate.
  6. Atomic swap of new and old .app via renamex_np(RENAME_SWAP)
     (atomic on APFS), with a non-power-failure-safe fallback for
     other filesystems.
  7. Delete staged.json + payload zip.

Exit codes mirror phlink::updater::mac::ApplyResult.

Tests: argument validation, missing-staged.json, missing-payload, and
SwapAppDirectories with two real temp dirs. Full SecCode signature
validation cannot be unit-tested without a real Developer-ID signed
fixture; those paths will be exercised in CI on the signed nightly
build (deferred to phase 10-08).

Helper is currently a build-only target; phase 10-07 will copy it
into the .dmg payload and phlink will exec it pre-relaunch via the
update settings UI (10-06).

30/30 phlink_updater_unittests pass.
Refs phlink phase 10-03.
